# Course 3 End Survey

Please complete the Course 3 end survey in Coursera.

The survey helps the course team understand what worked, what was confusing, and how learners used the course materials.

## What to Do

1. Open the survey item in Coursera.
2. Answer honestly based on your experience in Course 3.
3. Return to the course after submitting it.

There are no right or wrong programming answers on this page.

## Before You Go

Course 3 covered a lot of ground. If any of it has gone hazy, these are the pieces the next course builds on most directly:

- **[Modules](<../Module 1 - Libraries and Modules/12 - Modules Overview.webnb>)**, `import` and `export`, and [what a bundler does with them](<../Module 1 - Libraries and Modules/24 - Introduction to Bundlers.webnb>). Course 4 is written as modules from the first line.
- **[npm](<../Module 1 - Libraries and Modules/21 - Using npm to Manage Packages.webnb>)**, [`package.json`](<../Module 1 - Libraries and Modules/21a - The package.json File.webnb>), and installing a dependency, since React arrives that way.
- **[Servers and endpoints](<../Module 2 - Server-Side JavaScript/02 - Handling Requests and Responses.webnb>)**: sending a request, reading a response, and returning JSON.
- **[Semantic HTML and accessibility](<06 - Introduction to Accessibility and WCAG.webnb>)**, which do not stop mattering because a framework is generating the markup.

Everything else, the databases, the sessions, the operational transformations, is yours to reach for when a project needs it.

Thank you for working through it, and see you in Course 4.
